{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והשבותיך אל האדמה", :translit "v'hashavotikha el ha-adamah", :gloss "and I will bring you back to the land"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והשבותיך אל האדמה", :b "ארבע מלכיות"}], :frame {:text "The scheme of four successive empires—Babylon, Media, Greece, and Rome—that dominate Israel before the final redemption appears in Daniel's vision of four beasts (Daniel 7:1–28) and is enumerated as Babylon, Media, Greece, and Rome in the rabbinic chain of empires (Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Beshallah, Shirata 5). Genesis 28:15 records God's promise to Jacob that He will return him to the land; the equation of this phrase to 'four kingdoms' signals that the return encompasses Israel's survival through and beyond all four dominations.", :sources ["Daniel 7:1–28" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael Beshallah Shirata 5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "והשבותיך אל האדמה", :a-value 835, :b "ארבע מלכיות", :b-value 779, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:51.352962618Z", :model "glm-5.2"}